Scott wolf sportswriter inside USC blog  been covering USC for over 20 years how  did you react to the news that clay  Helton was keeping his job Scott I  probably felt a little sick to be honest  when I heard the news  how surprising was this it was coming  you know for a few days but if you'd had  told me a month ago he was coming back  it would have been surprising I mean  they've got a new president a new  athletic director it looks like they're  gonna make change and it's status quo  and everything's the same now and it's  almost like Lynn Swann is still the  athletic director and you know you don't  see any difference so I thought you know  they were going to clean house but  apparently they're not how much was and  I'm trying to figure this out of who was  available because usually if you make a  coaching change it's because you think  you're gonna get somebody who know  you're gonna get somebody I don't know  if money was a factor and or was the  person they wanted or persons they  wanted not going to be available well  I've heard that they did talk to Bob Stu  and I heard last night that there were  some issues with how much money they  were going to pay his coaching staff if  he were to come and I'm sure they put  out some feelers to Urban Meyer  especially with you know Reggie Bush and  Matt Leinart  sitting next to him every Saturday and  those guys are lobbying him to take the  USC job so you know I don't know how  committed they were to hiring a new  coach I mean it's nice and easy to you  know save millions of dollars on a  buyout but now they're in the situation  where they're going to lose millions of  dollars in ticket revenue and donations  because they've offended the fan base  like I've never seen it in the 20 plus  years I've been covering USC his play  Hilton good  he's good at sucking up to his bosses  the president and the athletic director  because he gave them game balls after  the UCLA game instead of keyed and  slovis school record 500 yards I don't  know how he's good I mean Mike bone was  defending him yesterday but they've been  one of the most 10 alights teams in the  nation the last three years so his job  this year was to clean up penalties so I  don't know how good he can be but also  you had this time frame as you point out  in your column there's like four days  where that elapsed before they said and  we're bringing back clay Helton so  something was happening in those four  days do we know what happened in those  four days they gave really vague answers  about that but my understanding was that  they were talking to Bob Stoops and they  probably were talking to some other  people too and I just don't understand  the timeframe I mean you did they give  themselves three or four days to hire a  new coach they've had you know a long  time to know this was coming so the  deadline seemed kind of weird to me they  should have been talking to someone the  last couple weeks but it just seemed  like they weren't ready to act and and I  don't know why and they're not being  very honest Mike bone said last night  that he didn't even talk to anybody else  and that's definitely not not the case  because otherwise they would have  announced Sunday morning that clay  Helton is coming back it's just still a  coveted job I think so I mean you're the  biggest program in the West and you're  in a pretty bad conference so you're  gonna have the most talent and you can  limit at 12 and be in the conversation  for the college football playoff and  you're not facing most two or three  tough opponents in the big ten or the  SEC so so I think it's a pretty easy job  to have and get to the college football  playoff but they're not even in the  national conversation for that anymore  yeah and they're talented team or at  least you saw you know pockets of talent  on this team if you were gonna make the  hire who would you have hired  I really liked Matt Campbell at Iowa  State I thought he would have been a  good hire for them because he's young  up-and-coming and they would probably  had to pay him as much of some of these  marquee guys but you know I don't even  know if they talked to him and it didn't  seem like they did so it just wasn't a  good search now if they've gotten Urban  Meyer that would have been great you  know everyone would have been happy and  I think Bob Stoops everyone would have  been happy but honestly any coach would  have been better I think in my eyes of a  fan so it would have been easy I I  always say you just hire a mannequin  because the mannequin won't do any  damage and clay Helton does do damn it  just a head coach so I think anybody  would have been better Scott thank you  for your time thank you for your  opinions I appreciate that  thanks Dan that Scott wolf he's a sports  writer for inside USC and it's been  covering USC for 20 years for more Dan  Patrick show tune in to audience Channel  239 on DirecTV stream for free on BR  live or download the Dan Patrick show  app  [Music]
 

